WEBVTT

00:00:00.035 --> 00:00:02.194
Suppose an agent was interrupted after submitting a

00:00:02.252 --> 00:00:03.320
request to a provider.

00:00:03.704 --> 00:00:05.828
You may not know whether the provider accepted it.

00:00:06.211 --> 00:00:08.545
Blindly resending can duplicate the effect.

00:00:08.986 --> 00:00:12.260
First inspect the job, logs, and durable records;

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:13.897
reconcile what happened.

00:00:14.338 --> 00:00:17.078
The same principle applies to a worker that may have

00:00:17.113 --> 00:00:19.191
committed changes before a session ended.

00:00:19.632 --> 00:00:24.183
Preserve valid work, identify the first unproven step, and

00:00:24.241 --> 00:00:27.144
only retry when the operation is safe to repeat.
